{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "id": "unusual-sessions",
  "title": "Unusual Sessions",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "f08427e1-49c5-4758-ace1-09ae33cee0dd",
      "question": "Using the first half of 2025 as the baseline, which 10 sessions from July 1, 2025 through January 30, 2026 were the most unusual among the 1,000 most liquid US stocks, and which features made each one unusual? Anomaly scores are neither forecasts nor explanations.",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-06T23:56:17.294598Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-06T23:56:41.861704Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Most Unusual Sessions (July 1, 2025 – January 30, 2026) among the 1,000 most liquid US stocks, using H1 2025 as baseline**\n\n| Rank | Date (session) | Ticker | Anomaly Score | Key Features Driving Unusualness (robust z-scores vs. H1 2025) |\n|------|----------------|--------|---------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1 | 2025-07-07 | BMNR | 2,450.5 | 5-day return **+480.4σ**, 20-day volatility **+100.2σ**, 1-day return **−3.3σ**, volume **+1.4σ** |\n| 2 | 2025-08-01 | DGNX | 438.1 | 1-day return **+359.7σ**, 20-day volatility **+108.9σ**, 5-day return **+152.8σ**, volume **−2.2σ** |\n| 3 | 2025-07-23 | ABVX | 277.1 | 1-day return **+283.6σ**, 5-day return **+117.6σ**, 20-day volatility **+85.2σ**, volume **+4.6σ** |\n| 4 | 2025-10-23 | BYND | 82.3 | 5-day return **+87.1σ**, 20-day volatility **+30.3σ**, 1-day return **−10.3σ**, volume **+1.3σ** |\n| 5 | 2025-08-04 | DGNX | 75.5 | 5-day return **+134.4σ**, 20-day volatility **+108.9σ**, 1-day return **−2.8σ**, volume **−2.1σ** |\n| 6 | 2025-08-05 | DGNX | 67.3 | 5-day return **+130.9σ**, 20-day volatility **+109.0σ**, 1-day return **−1.9σ**, volume **−1.7σ** |\n| 7 | 2025-10-22 | BYND | 66.0 | 5-day return **+85.1σ**, 20-day volatility **+30.0σ**, 1-day return **−1.8σ**, volume **+1.9σ** |\n| 8 | 2025-07-14 | BMNR | 64.4 | 20-day volatility **+101.0σ**, 5-day return **−12.2σ**, 1-day return **+0.6σ**, volume **+1.1σ** |\n| 9 | 2025-07-29 | ABVX | 63.8 | 5-day return **+118.4σ**, 20-day volatility **+85.3σ**, 1-day return **+2.4σ**, volume **+0.8σ** |\n| 10 | 2025-07-15 | BMNR | 62.5 | 20-day volatility **+100.9σ**, 5-day return **−12.9σ**, 1-day return **−1.8σ**, volume **+0.7σ** |\n\n**What the features mean (all are robust z-scores against the Jan–Jun 2025 baseline):**\n- **adjusted_return_1d**: Single-day price move relative to the asset’s own H1 2025 distribution.\n- **adjusted_return_5d**: Five-day cumulative return relative to the H1 2025 distribution.\n- **realized_volatility_20d**: 20-day rolling volatility relative to the H1 2025 distribution.\n- **log_volume_deviation_20d**: Log volume deviation from the asset’s own H1 2025 norm over 20 days.\n\n**Limitations**: Anomaly scores describe unusual observed feature combinations; they are not forecasts, probabilities, or evidence of a cause. Observed deviations are robust z-scores against the training window, not returns or percentages; they are descriptive reason codes and do not establish a cause or adverse event. The scan covered 991 assets in the liquid_1000 universe, with 97,838 training observations and 144,852 scoring observations.",
        "citations": []
      },
